### Runtime upload store — never commit ###
# These directories hold documents users upload through the application:
# passport scans, ID photos, profile pictures and finance receipts.
#
# They were tracked until V032. The files are AES-256-GCM encrypted at rest, but
# the dev-profile key that opens them lives in application-dev.properties, so
# committing them put readable student PII in the repository. Some paths also
# carry a student's name in the directory itself, which no encryption covers.
#
# The store is runtime state. It is restored from a filesystem backup, not from
# git — including uploads/logos/, which the admin UI re-uploads (the logo
# endpoint returns 404 rather than failing when it is absent).
uploads/

